WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.980
A lot of Hollywood bombs have detonated in
movie theaters in the last 20 years, but some

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.260
of these high-profile failures were made even
more embarrassing because of the movies that

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:09.660
beat them at the box office.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:13.940
Here are some big movies that went head-to-head
at the theaters - with the major release losing

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:14.440
hard.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.040
The Lone Ranger vs. Despicable Me 2

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:21.300
The director of Pirates of the Caribbean and
Disney teaming up again for another Johnny

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.020
Depp vehicle?

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.420
Sounds like a clear win.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.140
But according to The Hollywood Reporter, problems
with The Lone Ranger production set in almost

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:30.220
immediately, as the budget started to balloon.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:35.540
With a weak script, a 149-minute running time,
and a Depp performance that some reportedly

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.300
found racist, Lone Ranger bombed hard.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:43.380
It premiered the same weekend as Despicable
Me 2, and despite Ranger costing almost three

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:47.820
times as much to make, the animated film beat
it by more than $50 million.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:52.780
Disney ended up losing $150 million, and the
dream of the Lone Ranger franchise was over

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:54.140
before it really even started.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.660
Scream vs. Beavis and Butt-Head Do America

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:02.470
Scream was a surprisingly insightful takedown
of teen slasher films that went on to create

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:06.760
its own franchise and inspire the Scary Movie
films - but it didn't start huge.

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:11.520
In fact, it debuted in fourth place over its
opening weekend, beat out by the overall weekend

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.480
winner Beavis and Butt-Head Do America, which
grossed over $20 million.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.619
Scream's $6 million opening weekend didn't
scream success, but after getting very favorable

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:26.090
reviews and generating good word of mouth,
the movie ended up grossing $103 million domestically.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.580
"I'll send you a copy."

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.220
John Carter vs. The Lorax

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.920
Finding Nemo director Andrew Stanton was thrilled
to get a chance to bring his favorite sci-fi

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:41.740
book series to the big screen with his 2012
film John Carter, which combined romance and

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.820
deep space action.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.280
The film had high hopes, and Disney was ready
to make it a franchise.

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:51.440
But with a $250 million budget on a property
that most modern filmgoers aren't familiar

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.580
with, it wasn't surprising when rumors of
impending failure started spreading.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:59.860
According to Vulture, John Carter's first
trailers were met with tepid reactions, which

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:02.160
translated to some pretty weak ticket sales.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:06.880
On opening weekend, it was beat out by The
Lorax, which was in its second week in theaters

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.940
and had only received mediocre reviews.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:14.400
Lorax beat Carter by $8 million, and in the
end, Disney lost $200 million.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.480
The Fast and the Furious: Tokyo Drift vs.
Nacho Libre

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.280
You might not have many fond memories of the
comedy disappointment known as Nacho Libre,

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:27.400
but the filmmakers behind it will always get
to brag that they beat a Fast and the Furious

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:27.900
film.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:32.740
Tokyo Drift, the third entry of the high-intensity
action series, nearly stalled out.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:37.460
Featuring basically none of the main characters
from the first two movies and set in an entirely

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:41.980
new location, audiences seemed to be losing
interest in fast cars doing impossible things

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.000
on city streets.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:47.650
Tokyo Drift and Nacho Libre opened head to
head and the action franchise was fully expected

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.540
to beat the relatively low-budget comedy.

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:54.900
But Nacho Libre came out on top by a $5 million
margin - although they both still lost to

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.220
Pixar's Cars in its second week.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.060
Inferno vs. Boo!

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.320
A Madea Halloween

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:03.860
Tom Hanks and Ron Howard were probably not
thrilled to lose out to a Madea movie.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:08.140
The duo suffered from a greatly diminished
box office for their second Robert Langdon

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:13.720
film, Angels &amp; Demons, which grossed $133
million domestically compared to the $217

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:16.900
million haul enjoyed by its predecessor The
Da Vinci Code.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.160
Unfortunately, the third film, Inferno, did
even worse.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:25.640
It opened in second place at $17 million on
a weekend with no competition except the second

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:26.640
week of Boo!

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:27.620
A Madea Halloween.

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:31.800
In the end, Tyler Perry in drag easily outgrossed
America's dad, Tom Hanks.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:33.800
"Ahh!"

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:37.780
Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery
vs. Breakdown

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.200
Though he'd already had a hit with Wayne's
World, Austin Powers: International Man of

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:46.370
Mystery showed the world that Mike Myers didn't
need to rely on his previous success with

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:47.660
SNL to stay relevant.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.160
That being said, Powers was far from an instant
smash.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:55.110
On its opening weekend, the Myers movie lost
to the Kurt Russell thriller Breakdown.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:59.690
While Breakdown hasn't really stood the test
of time, it beat Austin Powers by about $3

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:01.440
million when they both debuted.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:05.710
The satirical British spy went on to do fine
at the box office, and then exploded on home

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:06.210
video.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:11.180
Austin Powers became a cult favorite and the
sequel opened at almost $55 million, quite

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.720
a bit higher than the original's $9 million.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.280
"Yeah baby!

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.400
Yeah!"

